{"term":"feedback","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:a228205c0dbe3f4e63","definition":"Critical assessment of a process or activity or of their results.","example":"After you hand in your essays, I will give both grades and feedback.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["estimation","assessment","critique","evaluation"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"usually","register":"uncountable, usually","wordFamily":["360 degree feedback","antifeedback","autofeedback","biofeedback","degenerative feedback","enterprise feedback management","feedback control","feedbacker","feedback loop","feedback transfer function","feedbacky","ice-albedo feedback","neurofeedback","postfeedback","regenerative feedback","video feedback"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/feedback#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f74acf566270f00d8b","definition":"The part of an output signal that is looped back into the input to control or modify a system.","example":"The fact that similar cortical abnormalities can be experimentally induced in monkeys has allowed Michael Merzenich and his colleagues in San Francisco to explore an animal model of focal dystonia, and to demonstrate the abnormal feedback in the sensory loop and the motor misfirings that, once started, grow relentlessly worse.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"usually","register":"uncountable, usually","wordFamily":["360 degree feedback","antifeedback","autofeedback","biofeedback","degenerative feedback","enterprise feedback management","feedback control","feedbacker","feedback loop","feedback transfer function","feedbacky","ice-albedo feedback","neurofeedback","postfeedback","regenerative feedback","video feedback"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/feedback#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:9be02217f91b590767","definition":"The high-pitched howling noise heard when there is a loop between a microphone and a speaker.","example":"A loud feedback screech blasted from a speaker on the wall. It was a hailing signal of some kind.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["audio feedback","Larsen effect","howlback","howlround"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"usually","register":"uncountable, usually","wordFamily":["360 degree feedback","antifeedback","autofeedback","biofeedback","degenerative feedback","enterprise feedback management","feedback control","feedbacker","feedback loop","feedback transfer function","feedbacky","ice-albedo feedback","neurofeedback","postfeedback","regenerative feedback","video feedback"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/feedback#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:48efa162bf4affd962","definition":"To generate the high-frequency sound by allowing a speaker to cause vibration of the sound generator of a musical instrument connected by an amplifier to the speaker.","example":"The show ended with a riot of feedbacking guitars.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["360 degree feedback","antifeedback","autofeedback","biofeedback","degenerative feedback","enterprise feedback management","feedback control","feedbacker","feedback loop","feedback transfer function","feedbacky","ice-albedo feedback","neurofeedback","postfeedback","regenerative feedback","video feedback"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/feedback#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e7d7b52dea32235117","definition":"To provide informational feedback to.","example":"His employees feedbacked him a lot more than he wanted.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["360 degree feedback","antifeedback","autofeedback","biofeedback","degenerative feedback","enterprise feedback management","feedback control","feedbacker","feedback loop","feedback transfer function","feedbacky","ice-albedo feedback","neurofeedback","postfeedback","regenerative feedback","video feedback"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/feedback#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6fd0bbbb904e3a2bd2","definition":"To convey by means of specialized communications channel.","example":"Customers feedbacked their complaints and some praise.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["360 degree feedback","antifeedback","autofeedback","biofeedback","degenerative feedback","enterprise feedback management","feedback control","feedbacker","feedback loop","feedback transfer function","feedbacky","ice-albedo feedback","neurofeedback","postfeedback","regenerative feedback","video feedback"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/feedback#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/ˈfiːdˌbæk/"},"wordFamily":["360 degree feedback","antifeedback","autofeedback","biofeedback","degenerative feedback","enterprise feedback management","feedback control","feedbacker","feedback loop","feedback transfer function","feedbacky","ice-albedo feedback","neurofeedback","postfeedback","regenerative feedback","video feedback"]}